    <!-- Pie y «¿Cómo se calcula?» (%1$d: palabras por minuto al teclear, Metrics.TYPING_WPM) -->
    <string name="met_footer">Everything is calculated on this phone from what Verbapp saves for each recording. None of it is sent.</string>
    <string name="met_how_button">How is this calculated?</string>
    <string name="met_how_title">How your metrics are calculated</string>
    <string name="met_how_body" tools:ignore="PluralsCandidate">Everything is calculated on this phone from what Verbapp already saves for each recording. Nothing is sent.\n\nRecorded: how long your recordings are, counted on the day you recorded.\nWords: the words in your transcripts (the current version).\nWords per minute: words ÷ minutes of transcribed audio.\nSaved by not typing: how long it would take to type those words by hand, at %1$d words per minute.\nStreak: consecutive days with at least one recording. If you haven\'t recorded yet today, it stays alive until midnight.\n\nToward your second brain: of what you recorded in the period, how much was transcribed, how much has a note, and how much you saved to your 0-Inbox folder.\n\nCosts: counted on the day the transcription or the note was made. “Charged” is what OpenRouter reported. “≈ Estimated” is the duration times the model\'s public rate and may differ from what you\'re charged. If you transcribed again, what the previous version cost is also counted while you keep it.\n\nPeople: how long each voice you named talks, not counting you. Names are only shown on this screen.</string>

